An RK611/RK06 *or* an RK611/RK07 disk drive subsystem is exactly that.
Just make sure you have the correct port switch (usually "A")
depressed on the RK07 panel, otherwise the CPU will not recognize the
drive. Also, you must have a logic plug installed (the little # 0 thru 7)
on the panel. 
 Make sure that you have a terminator installed on the last drive in the 
series also.
 Im not too adept at the controller addresses, but I think you need to
check that the controller status register is there (RKCS1 = 777440).
I have the ODT boot program around for that somewhere if you don't have
the boot prom for an RK07 also.. I could dig it up if you need it...



