In article <1991Jun5.141401.29280@murdoch.acc.Virginia.EDU>, blf2v@kelvin.seas.Virginia.EDU (Barry L. Farmer) writes:
> I have a MicroVax II, running VMS 5.3, to which I would like to add an RX-33 diskette
> drive.  I have an RQDX-3 controller to which two RD-54s are currently
> attached.  These drives are dua0 and dua1.  The installation
> instructions that came with the RX-33 describe how to configure the
> jumpers on the drive so that it will be drive 0 or 1, depending on
> whether it is the first or second diskette drive in the system.

  The RQDXn series of controllers will configure floppies at lower unit numbers
than fixed disks. So, you should wind up with unit 0=floppy, 1=RD54. 2=RD54.

  However, there are some complications depending on the mounting boxes in
use. If you have a BA23 box, you probably have an RQDXE disk extender and
an external RD54-Dn drive box. In that case, you may need to change jumpers
on the RQDXE extender card.

  If you have a BA123 box, you may need to change jumpers on the signal dis-
tribution board in slot 13.

  In general, your configuration should work "out of the box". I'd suggest
that you send me mail detailing your configuration and we can continue to
work this off-line.

